  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Solve each of the following quadratic equations by first putting the equation into standard form, and then completing the square:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2=2x+10$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1\\pm\\sqrt{11}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-2x-10&=0\\\\x^2-2x&=10\\\\x^2-2x+1&=11\\\\(x-1)^2&=11\\\\x-1&=\\pm\\sqrt{11}\\\\x&=1\\pm\\sqrt{11}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$4x-x^2=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2\\pm\\sqrt3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x+1&=0\\\\x^2-4x&=-1\\\\x^2-4x+4&=3\\\\(x-2)^2&=3\\\\x-2&=\\pm\\sqrt3\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2x^2=6x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt{15}}2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2-6x-3&=0\\\\x^2-3x-\\frac32&=0\\\\x^2-3x&=\\frac32\\\\x^2-3x+\\frac94&=\\frac{15}4\\\\\\left(x-\\frac32\\right)^2&=\\frac{15}4\\\\x-\\frac32&=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}2\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{15}}2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1{8-x}=\\dfrac{x}{14}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4\\pm\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne8$. Multiply both sides by $14(8-x)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}14&=x(8-x)\\\\x^2-8x+14&=0\\\\x^2-8x&=-14\\\\x^2-8x+16&=2\\\\(x-4)^2&=2\\\\x-4&=\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\x&=4\\pm\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values satisfy $x\\ne8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x-2=\\dfrac1x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1\\pm\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne0$. Multiply both sides by $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x-2)&=1\\\\x^2-2x-1&=0\\\\x^2-2x&=1\\\\x^2-2x+1&=2\\\\(x-1)^2&=2\\\\x-1&=\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\x&=1\\pm\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values are nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x+\\dfrac2x=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2\\pm\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne0$. Multiply both sides by $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+2&=4x\\\\x^2-4x+2&=0\\\\x^2-4x&=-2\\\\x^2-4x+4&=2\\\\(x-2)^2&=2\\\\x-2&=\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values are nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
  },
